{"id": "unknown-2026-11-19-011", "date": "2026-11-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "France’s first canal-top PV project goes online", "content": "<p>The 299 kW installation is expected to generate 404 MWh annually. Société du Canal de Provence estimates that its canal network could accommodate more than 50 MW of solar capacity, with potential annual generation of 70 GWh.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/19/frances-first-canal-top-pv-project-goes-online/\">France’s first canal-top PV project goes online</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/19/frances-first-canal-top-pv-project-goes-online/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-19-012", "date": "2026-11-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EU to launch €36 million funding call for advanced solar cell manufacturing", "content": "<p>The initiative aims to strengthen Europe's solar manufacturing industry by supporting high-efficiency solar cells, advanced production equipment, automated manufacturing processes and industrial-scale pilot production lines.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/19/eu-to-launch-e36-million-funding-call-for-advanced-solar-cell-manufacturing/\">EU to launch €36 million funding call for advanced solar cell manufacturing</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/19/eu-to-launch-e36-million-funding-call-for-advanced-solar-cell-manufacturing/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-19-013", "date": "2026-11-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indonesia could reach 96.7 GW of solar by 2029 with policy reforms", "content": "<p>IESR says Indonesia could achieve most of its 100 GW of solar by 2029 target through coordinated utility-scale procurement, rooftop PV deployment, diesel replacement and rural electrification, but warns regulatory and grid barriers need to be addressed.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/19/indonesia-could-reach-96-7-gw-of-solar-by-2029-with-policy-reforms/\">Indonesia could reach 96.7 GW of solar by 2029 with policy reforms</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/19/indonesia-could-reach-96-7-gw-of-solar-by-2029-with-policy-reforms/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-19-014", "date": "2026-11-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The U.S. solar manufacturing landscape in 2026", "content": "Having watched the global solar industry move from tens of megawatts annual demand to levels in excess of 500 GW by the early 2020s, the United States is finally making moves to create a silicon-based ecosystem to allow its demand for solar to be met by domestically made components. Finlay Colville examines the recent growth in US solar manufacturing.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine_usa", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/11/19/the-us-solar-manufacturing-landscape-in-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-19-015", "date": "2026-11-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cyber risk is becoming a procurement and bankability issue", "content": "New U.S. rules and cyber risks are forcing solar and storage buyers to weigh long-term software dependencies, data ownership, and equipment origin early in procurement rather than waiting until commissioning.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine_usa", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/11/19/cyber-risk-is-becoming-a-procurement-and-bankability-issue/", "type": "rss"}]}
