{"id": "first_solar-2026-11-19-017", "date": "2026-11-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": ["first_solar"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Aptera (SEV) completes its first customer solar EV — for its top crowdfunder", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/11/Aptera-first-delivery.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1280\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Aptera (SEV) has finished building its first solar electric vehicle for a paying customer. It’s going to Martin Hartono, the startup’s No. 1 “Accelerator” investor, and it’s being exported out of the US.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It’s a real milestone for a company that has pushed back its delive", "sources": [{"name": "electrek_solar", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/19/aptera-sev-first-solar-ev-customer-delivery-investor/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-19-018", "date": "2026-11-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The world’s biggest oil shock could give EVs and solar a boost", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/11/Kia-EV7-electric-SUV.jpeg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1400\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The longer the Strait of Hormuz crisis drags on, the more incentive countries have to get cars off oil and generate more power at home. That’s one of the big takeaways from the International Energy Agency’s (IEA) new “<a href=\"https://www.iea.org/reports/world-energy-outlook-2026\">World Energy Outlook 2026<", "sources": [{"name": "electrek_solar", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/18/the-worlds-biggest-oil-shock-could-give-evs-and-solar-a-boost/", "type": "rss"}]}
